          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Notes:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>overlay plots, show before and ofter</li>\n<li>2-3 strategies, or same strategy with different threshold</li>\n<li>ex.  one patient every x # hours</li>\n<li>show how much transferring is required to meaningfully lower occupancy (LJ)</li>\n<li>ex. you find out you have to transfer 20 patients per day</li>\n<li>can explain why we used QuantReg, looking at dist</li>\n<li>run sim over different thresholds, and show how it changes</li>\n<li>dont use predicted LOS completely, follow real path both ways, don't force them to stay whole predicted LOS</li>\n<li>the better the model is, the less patients will need to move to make an impact</li>\n<li>do the same thing, but remaining LOS is their actual LOS based on their traj, keep same logic</li>\n<li>annotate our plots, point out peaks, when resources are full</li>\n<li>one plot with diff threshold for transfer, and show how diff resource utilization/occupancy plays out, refernce ridge plots</li>\n<li>diff wait times with different threshold/assumptions, show what it takes to lower wait time by x units</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"-and-show-how-the-different-hospitals-respondfunction-in-response-to-that\">- and show how the different hospitals respond/function in response to that ^</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>for LOS, residual plot, plot actual vs observed, bland-altman</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
